at 12:00 PM on 9/23/2026 due to transitioning to Michigan LARA\nEastern Upper Peninsula Transportation Advisory Committee\nBoard Vacancy Notices\nApplication of Interest\nNovember 3rd, 2026 General Election Information\nWhat's on the Ballot?\nEARLY VOTING\nEarly voting for the General Election will begin Saturday, October 24, 2026 and End Sunday November 1st, 2026 from 8:00 AM to 4:00 PM at the following locations:\nCity of Sault Ste. Marie and Soo Township\nSoo Township Hall\n639 3-1/2 Mile Rd\nSault Ste. Marie, MI 49783\nBay Mills; Bruce; Chippewa; Dafter; DeTour; Drummond Island; Hulbert; Kinross; Pickford; Raber; Rudyard; Sugar Island; Superior; Trout Lake; Whitefish:\nKinross Township Hall\n4884 Curtis Street\nKincheloe, MI 49788\nElection Results\nAugust 4th, 2026- Primary Election\nOfficial August 4th Election - Summary\n​\nOfficial August 4th Election - Statement of Votes Cast\n​\n​ View past election results click here ​\nOnline Search Services\nRegister of Deeds Search\nName searches, deeds, liens, mortgages, land contracts, and other documents pertaining to real estate in Chippewa County may be performed online..........\nGIS Online Map\nGIS Map of EUP including: Chippewa and Mackinac Counties, and the City of Sault Ste. Marie\n​\nParcel Record Search\nProperty descriptions, taxable status, owner and taxpayer names, mailing and situs addresses.....\nUpcoming Meetings\n2026 Meeting Schedule\n​\nMeetings are generally held in the 91st District Courtroom, 2nd Floor of the County Building, located at 325 Court Street, Sault Ste. Marie, MI unless otherwise noted. The following meeting are available for public attendance. The Board of Commissioners Regular Monthly Meeting will be available via Zoom, please join us by clicking the meeting below for the Zoom instructions. ​\n* If Court Proceedings are in session, the meeting(s) will be held in t he 50th Circuit Courtroom, at the Courthouse, located at 319 Court Street.\nClick Here to receive Regular Board, and Finance Committee, Agendas and Packets via Email\nOpioid Steering Fund Committee Meeting\nMicrosoft Teams Link\nMonday October 12th 2026, at 3:30 p.m.\nChippewa County Health Department - St. Mary's Room\nFinance, Claims and Accounts Committee\nAgenda\nTuesday, October 13th, 2026 at 5:30 p.m.\nCounty Building- 91st Courtroom\nRegular Board Meeting\nZoom Information\nAgenda\nThursday, October 15th, 2026, at 5:30 p.m.\nCounty Building- 91st Courtroom\nSpecial Meeting Notice\nChippewa county Sheriff Appointment Committee\nAgenda\nThursday, November 12th, 2026, at 12:00 p.m.\nCounty Building- 91st Courtroom\nCentral Dispatch Board of Directors\n2026 MEETING SCHEDULE\nLEPT (Local Emergency Planning Team)\n2026 MEETING SCHEDULE\nLEPC (Local Emergency Planning Committee)\n2026 MEETING SCHEDULE\n​\n​\nVeteran Affairs\n2026 MEETING SCHEDULE\nNews & Information\nFAQs about the Michigan Legal Help Website\nApplication of Interest for Board Vacancies\n​\nBoard Adopted Redistricting Plan\n​\n​\nSign Up For Smart911\nDog License by Mail\nMeetings & Minutes\n2026 Meeting Schedule\nForms\n2026 Holiday Schedule\nContact Us\nElectronic Device Policy\nDriving Directions\n​\nbottom of page",
